 not looking at all you may see  something as basic as pawn to h3 and  then simply black can come in and it's  checking that game over that easy now  they may completely ignore the whole  situation and move something like Bishop  to b2 and from here we can simply  capture on h2 and then let's say they  recapture with their knight then we can  simply bring our queen in and they only  have one move and that's to bring their  pawn to g3 and then we can recapture for  checkmate you may see them recapture  with their rook and then from here we  can recapture and they cannot recapture  with their Knight obviously if they  capture with their night then we can  come in and same story they're gonna  have to move their pawn to g3 and we can  easily checkmate  so from here they may try a different  move they can try to develop they can  they may move to g7 where we can just  move our rope to g8 but all in all we're  going to end up taking their Bishop on  f1 we're gonna be up in material and  their entire structure is going to be  completely messed up so White has the  option if they can mess up their whole  structure or get checkmate it pretty  easy and the game that actually played  ended up where they just move their pawn  to h3 and I just quickly came in and  checked made it on g3 and they never saw  it coming so if you see the birds  opening and you want to try this out I  think it's a pretty nifty trap so hope  you guys enjoyed I'll see you guys next  video

